> greg@gagme.uucp (Gregory Gulik) writes ( 2:59 pm  Dec 29, 1989 in stasys:rec.games.hack): 
> Subject: Beginners at nethack completely con
> Ok, we've been playing this game here off and on for a couple
> weeks now and we can't figure out one thing.
> 
> what does the color of a potion have to do with it's function?
> 
> For example, during one game, the pink potion was a potion
> of invisibility, and a couple games later when I got another
> pink potion, it was a potion of restore ability.
> 
> Are there any rules for this?

Yes, there are rules. The color of a potion, the name of a scroll and
so on arent't allways the same. If you start a new game, every item
gets its description, e.g. a scroll called "READ ME" may be an identify
scroll. For this game, all scrolls "READ ME" are identify scrolls.
But if you die and start a new game things are completely different.

